{
  "id": "ss.char.hex",
  "name": "Hex",
  "description": "A survivor in cell-shaped plating — the same hexagon the hive builds with, worn by something the hive no longer counts. Six-sided helmet, a chest plate tiled with cells, and on its back a brood vent: the puckered plate that pushes out grubs, carried the way another survivor would carry a pack. Two grubs ride it already, one on the shoulder and one at the hip, and they never stop moving, because a grub does not know it is not at home. The arms are the slightest on the roster; this one does not hit anything itself, it sends things. Same dead organ as the rest, same place, and the same feelers. Bare chitin cold slate, orchid plate over it. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
